EverQuest Legends introduced a number of new action abilities, one of which is referred to as "Rituals". 

Rituals are an alternative way for spellcasting classes to commit select spells to memory that are able to be cast even when that class is not part of your current active loadout.

To access rituals press "L" to open the 'Actions' window, then select the "Rituals" tab.

=== Requirements ===
* In order for the ritual version of an eligible spell to be initially created, a player must reach the level required to scribe the spell. For example once you reach level 5 on a cleric and scribe the spell "Gate", it will automatically create the Ritual version. If multiple classes gain access to a common spell that can become a ritual, whichever class reaches the minimum required level to scribe the spell is what will create the ritual version.

* You must be out of combat and in a 'resting' state to cast a ritual.

* Rituals will take 20 seconds to cast, regardless of what the individual spell descriptions state.

* Upon completion of the ritual, player will lose ALL mana. 

== Notes ==
* While it is possible to cast a ritual even when the original spell is available on a class in a players active loadout, it is not recommended as it will still result in draining 100% of your mana pool.

